{"school":{"dbn":"27Q210","name":"J.H.S. 210 Elizabeth Blackwell","boro":"Queens","district":"27","district_label":"District 27","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1484,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"93-11 101 AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11416","phone":"718-843-2260","website":"ms210q.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/65999","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Elizabeth Blackwell MS 210Q holds the unwavering belief that all children have the inalienable right to a quality education in a safe and nurturing environment, which allows them to develop into cognitive, self-directed, socially responsible, young adults.  We believe in setting high expectations for our students and enriching their lives by providing a holistic experience. Using different data points and SEL techniques, we have reimagined the student experience, which is rooted in reading, writing and mathematical thinking.  We also offer sports, Accerated Regents classes in Algebra, Living Environment, US History, and ELA, as well as robust Arts (Theater, Dance, Visual Arts, Music) Programs to expose students to different forms of expression and pathways to success. Additionally, we also have 40+ After-School Programs to support your child's development in formative years (Academic enrichment, Sports, as well as SEL). Furthermore, by collaborating with various stakeholders, including our CBO partner, Beacon, our vision is to prepare our students to meet and exceed the challenges of college and the workforce, attaining the highest levels of equitable, success possible.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"A to Rockaway Blvd","bus":"Q11, Q112, Q21, Q24, Q37, Q41, Q52-SBS, Q53-SBS, Q7, Q8, QM15","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Ozone Park","latitude":40.6843,"longitude":-73.847647,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year"